{start_of_verse}
[G]The postman came and brought a letter
It was from her [C]boy who went [D7]away
She gave him [C]up to join the [G]colors
Each time he writes [D7]I hear her [G]pray
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Dear God watch [C]o’er my boy in [G]service
Help him win his [D7]victory
And when [C]this cruel war is [G]over
Bring him safely back to me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Then came the day they walked together
To the [C]train that took him [D7]away
She knew her [C]boy would be a [G]hero
Her smilin eyes [D7]just seemed to [G]say
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Now soldier boy don’t e’er forger her
She prays to [C]God for you each [D7]day
That harm may [C]never [G]overtake you
While you are fighting [D7]far [G]away
{end_of_verse}
